// RFC 0016 K4 "Families match ports" and K5's surface model: LightmappedGeneric
// in the combos the core's `lightmapped` family claims: base texture, the flat
// lightmap, $color, vertex color and alpha, $alpha, alpha test and
// translucency; the bumped lightmap pages (RNM) under a bump map or an ssbump,
// $nodiffusebumplighting; env maps with $envmapmask, base and normal map alpha
// masks, tint, contrast, saturation and fresnel; detail (TextureCombine modes 0
// and 1); self-illumination with a tint. The legacy port draws them (run with
// --extra-arg=-vklegacylightmapped; its pixels are judged against the retail
// D3D9 bytecode) and records the port pixels the family suite compares with
// (tools/render/family_port_pixels.py). Quads are in clip space (identity
// transforms), so the eye is at the origin. The cases the family does not
// claim yet (bump masks, masked blending, fog through the harness) stay in
// ../forced/lightmappedgeneric_native_combos.vdf. WorldVertexTransition's two
// layers are here: the vertex alpha's blend, $blendmodulatetexture's window,
// and $bumpmap2 at $bumptransform's coordinates, flat and ssbump. The bumped
// cases carry no $blendmodulatetexture: off the port's vertex fast path (any
// $bumptransform) the D3D9 helper uploads the blend mask transform only with
// $maskedblending, so the window is read through whatever that constant holds
// (zero in the harness, the previous draw's value in a game): undefined, and
// the core reads it at the base coordinates as the fast path defines.
"LegacyShaderCases"
{
